"""Readable autonomous dataset and validation reports, without manifest dumps."""
from .common import *
import shutil

def fmt(v,n=5):return '—' if v is None else f'{v:.{n}f}'
def link(name):return f'[{name}](../experiments/{RUN}/{name})'

def render(state,reason):
 audit=read(OUT/'reuse-audit.json');complete=read(OUT/'completion.json') if (OUT/'completion.json').exists() else {};phase=read(OUT/'phase-state.json') if (OUT/'phase-state.json').exists() else {};index=read(OUT/'dataset-index.json') if (OUT/'dataset-index.json').exists() else [];counts=collections.Counter(x['partition'] for x in index);shard=read(OUT/'dataset-shards.json') if (OUT/'dataset-shards.json').exists() else {};forecast=read(OUT/'feasibility-forecast.json') if (OUT/'feasibility-forecast.json').exists() else None;dataset=read(OUT/'dataset-completion.json') if (OUT/'dataset-completion.json').exists() else None;analysis=read(OUT/'analysis.json') if (OUT/'analysis.json').exists() else None;fits=[read(p) for p in (OUT/'fit-results').glob('*.json')];native=rows(OUT/'matches.jsonl');reuse=read(OUT/'reuse-primary.json')
 text=f'# Belief-learning dataset v1\n\nState: **{state}**. Updated {iso()}.\n\n{reason}\n\n'
 text+=f'This dataset keeps original Hydrapple as observer against 37 frozen library lists. Both actors use the unchanged embedding-final Unown package (submission 57834515), conditional argmax, native BO3 and the verified starting-order/legal-memory adapter. No belief model influences collection. Native deals are independent; policy seeds do not control native shuffles.\n\n'
 text+='Source-repair005 preserves failed execution003 and resume004, their diagnostics and both earlier startup failures. The exact allocator repair remains unchanged. Resume004 later hit a separate legal-observer defect: Crispin emptied the deck while putting its last Energy into hand; official ShuffleDeck emits no Shuffle event for an empty deck, leaving the old Crispin attachment-source flag active. A later ordinary hand attachment was incorrectly deducted from the empty deck. The minimal repair expires that hint at certified deck exhaustion. Negative-count, public-count, legal-fact and target-alignment guards remain strict. '+link('official-attachment-semantics.json')+'.\n\n'
 text+='There are now four interrupted histories without complete recoverable data. The prior user choice to leave missing histories unreplaced is preserved. Only the original frozen8/16-BO3/list curves remain fully recoverable. This continuation collects67 previously unissued training IDs in original order, runs14 unchanged fits and15 fixed-validation evaluations including A, and leaves32/64/128 unavailable. The newly failing completed match is recovered offline from retained legal history/native diagnostics. Existing records outside the eligible subsets remain archived. A correctness failure now blocks new dispatches immediately and drains already-started BO3 before stopping workers, with the resource watchdog still active. No actor, model recipe, deck, decoder, reward, sample seed or deadline changes. '+link('recovery-registration.json')+'; '+link('recovery-reconciliation.json')+'.\n\n'
 text+='## Historical reuse and distribution\n\nThe audit distinguishes full legal histories with aligned hidden targets from compact outcome records. It inspected all 296 belief-development matches and all 100 retained screen replays. The screen’s native target frames are in its separate visualization field, not in player observations. There are no duplicate match IDs among the 396 audited matches.\n\n'
 text+=f'- Primary training reuse: **{audit["primary_reused"]} BO3** ({audit["legacy_primary"]} belief histories and {audit["screen_primary"]} screen histories).\n- Auxiliary archive: **{audit["auxiliary_BO3"]} round-robin BO3**, with both viewpoints grouped under their original match IDs. They are excluded from the primary benchmark.\n- {audit["compact_screen_outcomes_not_histories"]} other screen attempts have compact outcomes without retained reusable full histories; they do not count as dataset samples.\n- All previously inspected matches are training-only. The 296 existing reserved IDs are retained once in locked test; their outcomes/targets were not inspected for this design. Another 296 fresh locked-test IDs complete that partition.\n\n'
 text+='The screen and prior belief collector differ only in the input ordering of the anchor’s identical 60-card multiset. New games pin the exact previous belief-collector order. The actor represents own-deck copies as counters and sorts them in its encoder; retained screen-prefix parity passed. Both original ordered-input hashes remain documented in ordered-list-audit.json. Mirrors use one observer viewpoint selected without outcomes; other viewpoints and all game rounds remain in the same match group. Historical dataset counts are totals reused, not extra fresh games. Source policy/deck/SDK hashes, exact observation/target completeness and prior use are recorded per imported match in '+link('inventory.json')+'.\n\n'
 text+='## Allocation and current completion\n\n| Partition | Planned BO3/list | Planned total | Committed valid BO3 | New attempts planned |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
 for part,n,total,new in (('training',128,4736,4372),('validation',16,592,592),('locked-test',16,592,592)):text+=f'| {part} | {n} | {total} | {counts[part]} | {new} |\n'
 text+=f'\nOriginal target: 5,920 BO3; original new allocation5,556 attempts. Recovery deliberately leaves the four lost histories missing and does not collect IDs belonging only to unavailable32/64/128 subsets. Expected archive after eligible collection:3,518 records, including all592 required16/list training histories plus extra previously collected training records. Reuse364; cumulative native starts expected3,158; no replacements or quota refilling. Recorded native attempts/results so far: {len(list((OUT/"issued").glob("*.json")))}/{len(native)}; successful {sum(x["status"]=="DONE" for x in native)}, failed {sum(x["status"]!="DONE" for x in native)}. Unresolved attempts are listed in completion.json. The original first two validation matches passed integration. The first two remaining scheduled training IDs also check recovery-path integration; neither is an extra native match.\n\n'
 text+='Nested training subsets contain 8, 16, 32, 64 and 128 BO3 per list (296, 592, 1,184, 2,368 and 4,736 independent BO3). Each subset and final partition is exactly balanced by initial chooser within list. Schedules are shuffled; policies retain the legal right to choose the actual starter. Original eight/list histories anchor the smallest subset. Retained screen histories are then used before new matches, within chooser-balanced nested prefixes.\n\n'
 text+='## Reusable records and isolation\n\nEach indexed compressed shard contains up to 16 whole BO3 records. Three separate components store (1) full ordered legal callback observations/events and responses, including forced selections; (2) aligned hidden hand/draw/prize counts plus physical hand serials at up to 24 hash-selected genuine decisions/game; and (3) policy/adapter/SDK/deck/schema provenance, chooser, actual starters, outcomes and timing. Raw legal inputs contain no diagnostic targets. All library card IDs define the query universe, independently of the actual hidden hand. Target joins verify native pre-action state keys, public counts and physical known-card bounds.\n\n'
 text+='New collection uses the same frozen actors. The observer runs after collection, and its corrected Metang/Dwebble/Crispin/Drakloak/provenance semantics are reused unchanged. All old fact/reset/deduplication checks remain. The exact marginal-distribution extension is checked against the frozen A presence/mean/variance implementation at every labelled training/validation point. A material correctness error stops collection, preserving the failed ID and all in-flight attempts. No public count is overwritten to fit truth.\n\n'
 text+='Locked-test integrity checks only verify schema, alignment, legal count bounds, frozen policy and schedule identity. The model dataset loader rejects locked-test inputs and targets, and preprocessing rejects that partition. Test targets are sealed after collection. No test model scores, outcome exploration or model selection are authorized. A valid raw dataset does not imply that model fitting or validation has finished.\n\n'
 text+=f'Original full dataset complete: **False**. Committed records/eligible-subset integrity verified: **{bool(dataset and dataset.get("valid"))}**. Test committed: **{counts["locked-test"]}/592**; test model scores: **0**. Whole-BO3 grouping is preserved for every view and game.\n\n'
 text+='The raw archive supports future legal-history encoders and alternative marginal count targets. Its sampled target points do not provide labels at arbitrary unrecorded decisions, and the records do not establish counterfactual simulator support. Derived marginal predictions are not automatically joint hidden-world samples.\n\n'
 text+='## Resources and feasibility\n\nCaps are 64 CPU-core hours across preparation/collection/preprocessing/fitting/analysis, 48 UTC elapsed hours from execution launch, and at most four active compute threads. Three single-thread collection workers leave one thread for controller/serialization; feature jobs run while actors are idle, and supervised fitting uses three threads with no concurrent collection. Supervised fitting has a separate aggregate 20 CPU-core-hour cap and family/size-specific per-fit caps (600 s Bayesian, 900 s trees, and 500+46n s for both neural families, where n is training BO3/list), with recovery/export reserves inside the caps. Curated private artifacts are capped at 16 GiB; detailed diagnostics have a separate 2 GiB cap, at most 100 preselected successful full replays and first 10 examples/signature. No permanent power-plan change is made.\n\n'
 if (OUT/'lifecycle.json').exists():text+='UTC launch/deadline: '+read(OUT/'lifecycle.json')['started_at_utc']+' / '+read(OUT/'lifecycle.json')['deadline_utc']+'.\n\n'
 if forecast:text+=f'Original full-plan first allocated batch (historical forecast, not the recovery forecast): {forecast["first_batch_BO3"]} BO3. Mean collection/integrity cost {forecast["mean_native_CPU_seconds"]:.2f} CPU s/BO3; feature extraction {forecast["mean_feature_CPU_seconds"]:.2f} CPU s/BO3. Conservative projected totals: {forecast["conservative_total_CPU_hours"]:.2f} CPU-core hours, {forecast["conservative_elapsed_hours"]:.2f} elapsed hours, {forecast["curated_storage_GiB"]:.2f} GiB curated storage. Measured-plan feasibility gate passed: **{forecast["complete_plan_fits"]}**.\n\n'
 if (OUT/'recovery-forecast.json').exists():
  rf=read(OUT/'recovery-forecast.json');text+=f'Recovery forecast: **{rf["remaining_elapsed_hours"]:.2f} remaining elapsed hours**, **{rf["cumulative_CPU_hours"]:.2f} cumulative CPU-core hours**, based on retained collection/feature timings and all eligible fit caps; fits original deadline/caps: **{rf["fits_original_budget"]}**. '+link('recovery-forecast.json')+'.\n\n'
 if complete:text+=f'Measured execution CPU: {complete.get("measured_execution_CPU_seconds",0)/3600:.3f} core hours; measured preparation components: {complete.get("measured_preparation_CPU_seconds",0)/3600:.3f} core hours. Fully collected/encoded training subset sizes: {complete.get("fully_collected_training_subset_sizes",[])}/{complete.get("fully_encoded_training_subset_sizes",[])} BO3/list; minimum chooser-balanced coverage by partition: {complete.get("minimum_balanced_BO3_per_list",{})}. Actual final controller-accounted CPU: {complete.get("final_CPU_seconds",complete["CPU_seconds"])/3600:.3f} core hours, including the clearly labelled preparation budget charge; elapsed {complete.get("final_elapsed_seconds",complete["elapsed_seconds"])/3600:.3f} hours. Native issued/completed/failed: {complete["native_issued"]}/{complete["native_completed"]}/{complete["native_failed"]}. Measured fitting child CPU including process startup/export: {complete["fit_CPU_seconds"]/3600:.3f} core hours. Curated/detail storage: {complete["curated_bytes"]/1024**3:.3f}/{complete["detail_bytes"]/1024**3:.3f} GiB. Measured preparation components and conservative unmetered-work charge are separate in preparation-charge.json; the charge is not presented as an invented actual CPU measurement.\n\n'
 conversion=read(OUT/'conversion-cost.json') if (OUT/'conversion-cost.json').exists() else None
 feature_records=[read(p) for p in (OUT/'feature-results').glob('*.json')]
 text+=f'Measured historical audit CPU: {audit["CPU_seconds"]:.2f} s. Curated-shard historical conversion CPU: {fmt(conversion.get("CPU_seconds") if conversion else None,2)} s. Native match workers plus integrity: {sum(x["CPU_core_seconds"]+x.get("integrity_CPU_seconds",0) for x in native)/3600:.3f} core hours, with worker startup recorded separately. Feature computation: {sum(x["CPU_seconds"] for x in feature_records)/3600:.3f} core hours; feature loading/target joins/cache export: {sum(x["total_CPU_seconds"]-x["CPU_seconds"] for x in feature_records)/3600:.3f} core hours. Full online timing feature passes are recorded separately.\n\n'
 text+='Evidence: '+', '.join(link(n) for n in ('registration.json','recovery-registration.json','recovery-reconciliation.json','allocator-parity-gate.json','failed-history-replay-gate.json','official-attachment-semantics.json','runtime-compatibility.md','inventory.json','reuse-audit.json','auxiliary-manifest.json','reserved-ID-reconciliation.json','split-manifest.json','training-subsets.json','collection-schedule.json','schema.json','dataset-shards.json','dataset-completion.json','completion.json'))+'. Private records, weights, SDK assets and model artifacts remain outside Git.\n'
 DATA_REPORT.write_text(text)
 model=f'# Belief classifier learning curves\n\nState: **{state}**. Updated {iso()}.\n\n{reason}\n\n'
 model+=f'Original full dataset complete: **False**. Eligible subsets verified: **{bool(dataset and dataset.get("valid"))}**. Finished authorized supervised fits: **{sum(x["state"]=="COMPLETE" for x in fits)}/14**. Original35-fit plan remains incomplete. Locked-test evaluations: **0**. Model scores below are fixed-validation/model-selection evidence, not final test performance. An incomplete fit is not a scientific negative result.\n\n'
 model+='## Frozen comparison\n\nA is the unchanged legal conditional-allocation baseline, extended to exact count marginals and checked against its existing moments. Bayesian weighting uses the same six alpha/beta settings and selects validation deck log loss, with one final reveal ledger per training BO3. Trees, the two-layer width-128 feedforward network, and the single width-128 GRU use seeds 11 and 29 at each fixed training size. Both seeds are retained. Each neural model is below one million parameters.\n\n'
 model+='Trees and the feedforward network receive identical fixed current public/history-summary and per-card feature matrices. Card identity is an eight-bit exact query index; fixed signed sketches summarize legal copy/event counts. No text embedding API or new text vectors are used. Both models have the same A probabilities/count distributions. The GRU adds the full ordered encoded current-game callback sequence, including forced observations; state resets to zero at every new game. Only permitted legal deck facts cross game boundaries. No early prefix is discarded. The event encoding is lossy; a null GRU result would not rule out all possible history encodings.\n\n'
 model+='The tree method is 32-stage stochastic gradient boosting of multi-output depth-three regression trees on proper masked multiclass negative gradients. Each stage uses a cyclic balanced eight BO3/list batch; all training BO3 are covered at least twice at every eligible size; the original32/64/128 sizes remain unavailable. All registered labelled queries participate; legally deterministic count cells have zero gradient. No count class is rebalanced. Neural models use AdamW at 0.001, six maximum epochs, validation-NLL patience three and fixed loss weights. All learned models predict residual logits around A; the legal count support includes every frozen multiplicity up to 17. Recovery checkpoints are diagnostic, not retrospectively selected validation winners; neural best-epoch retention follows the frozen early-stop rule.\n\n'
 model+='The common legal support mask and normalization apply to every method. No joint zone-total projection is applied. The report retains remaining expected-zone-total errors and known-fact/support violations; marginal distributions need not define a coherent complete hidden world. Proper deck and count log losses are averaged by query→decision→game→BO3→chooser/population. Primary uncertain-hand Brier uses the same A-defined [0.10,0.90] subset for all models. Primary weights are the 30-list n/82 pool; secondary weights cover all 37 lists at n/100.\n\n'
 model+='The 592 validation BO3 are fixed, with eight per initial chooser/list. Paired 20,000 whole-match bootstrap samples use identical resampling across methods, sizes and seeds within list/chooser strata. Seeds are not independent matches: both individual scores and within-BO3 mean metrics are reported. Intervals condition on fitted models, omit full retraining uncertainty, and are nominal descriptive intervals across multiple learning-curve comparisons. Later-game participation is outcome-dependent and game/stage breakdowns are descriptive.\n\n'
 if analysis:
  model+='## Validation learning curves\n\n![Validation learning curves](../experiments/'+RUN+'/learning-curves.png)\n\n'
  for pop in ('eligible','full_field'):
   model+='### '+('Primary n/82' if pop=='eligible' else 'Secondary n/100')+'\n\n| Model / independent training BO3 | Uncertain Brier | Difference vs A [paired 95% interval] | Deck accuracy | Deck log loss | ECE | Hand/draw/prize MAE |\n|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n'
   for key,values in analysis['point'][pop].items():
    contrast=analysis['minus_A'][pop].get(key,{}).get('uncertain_brier');diff='—' if not contrast else f'{contrast["difference"]:+.6f} [{contrast["CI95"][0]:+.6f}, {contrast["CI95"][1]:+.6f}]';label=key
    if key!='A':label+=' / '+str(37*int(key.split('-n')[1].split('-')[0]))
    model+='| '+label+' | '+fmt(values.get('uncertain_brier'))+' | '+diff+' | '+fmt(values.get('deck_accuracy'))+' | '+fmt(values.get('deck_log_loss'))+' | '+fmt(values.get('ECE'))+' | '+' / '.join(fmt(values.get(k)) for k in ('hand_MAE','deck_MAE','prize_MAE'))+' |\n'
   model+='\n'
  model+='### Every opponent list at the largest completed sizes\n\nAll per-deck, game/stage, count-consistency, coverage and seed-specific values are retained in '+link('analysis.json')+'. Missing metrics retain explicit population coverage; partial fits do not substitute another sample.\n\n'
  common_sizes=[n for n in SIZES if all(k in analysis['point']['eligible'] for k in [f'Bayes-n{n}-s0']+[f'{f}-n{n}-seedmean' for f in ('Trees','MLP','GRU')])]
  if common_sizes:
   n=max(common_sizes);chosen=['A',f'Bayes-n{n}-s0']+[f'{f}-n{n}-seedmean' for f in ('Trees','MLP','GRU')]
   model+=f'Largest fully matched learning-curve size: **{n} BO3/list**. Cells below show uncertain-hand Brier / deck accuracy.\n\n| Opponent list / family | '+' | '.join(chosen)+' |\n|---|'+'---|'*len(chosen)+'\n'
   for deck in analysis['per_deck']:
    model+='| '+deck['deck'][:10]+' '+deck['archetype']+' | '+' | '.join(fmt(deck['methods'][k].get('uncertain_brier'))+' / '+fmt(deck['methods'][k].get('deck_accuracy'),3) for k in chosen)+' |\n'
   model+='\n| Game or stage (primary pool) | '+' | '.join(chosen)+' |\n|---|'+'---|'*len(chosen)+'\n'
   for group,values in analysis['breakdowns'].items():
    model+='| '+group+' | '+' | '.join(fmt(values['eligible'][k]['point'].get('uncertain_brier'))+' (coverage '+fmt(values['eligible'][k]['coverage'].get('uncertain_brier'),2)+')' for k in chosen)+' |\n'
   model+='\n| Model | H/D/P expected-total MAE | Card-total violation MAE / fraction | Impossible-count mass |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n'
   for k in chosen:
    v=analysis['point']['eligible'][k];model+='| '+k+' | '+' / '.join(fmt(v.get(m)) for m in ('hand_total_MAE','deck_total_MAE','prize_total_MAE'))+' | '+fmt(v.get('card_total_violation_MAE'))+' / '+fmt(v.get('card_total_violation_fraction'))+' | '+fmt(v.get('support_mass_violation'),8)+' |\n'
   model+='\n'
  model+='## Decision\n\n'
  promising=[]
  for family in ('Bayes','Trees','MLP','GRU'):
   key='Bayes-n16-s0' if family=='Bayes' else family+'-n16-seedmean';c=analysis['minus_A']['eligible'].get(key,{}).get('uncertain_brier');coverage=analysis['coverage']['eligible'].get(key,{}).get('uncertain_brier',0)
   if c and coverage>=1-1e-8 and c['difference']<0 and c['CI95'][1]<0:promising.append((c['difference'],family))
  if state not in ('COMPLETE','COMPLETE_ELIGIBLE_CURVES'):model+='The planned comparison is incomplete. Reported completed fits remain useful validation evidence, but no family is declared inferior because a fit or execution budget ended. Completed balanced learning-curve sizes are recorded in completion.json. No locked-test scoring or automatic follow-up occurs.\n\n'
  elif promising:
   promising.sort();family=promising[0][1];model+=f'{family} at 16 BO3/list has the strongest eligible-pool point reduction among families with a negative paired interval upper bound. This is a validation-selected hypothesis. A separate authorized confirmation could use its frozen seed-11 representative (the seed was predetermined, not chosen as the better seed); Bayesian fitting is deterministic. The two-seed mean shown is a mean of validation metrics, not an evaluated model ensemble. No locked-test access or deployment follows automatically.\n\n'
  else:model+='No largest-size family establishes an uncertain-hand Brier improvement over A under the paired validation intervals and complete-coverage requirement. Preserve the dataset and fitted models; no locked-test scoring, PPO, new collection or follow-up is launched. This does not prove that all supervised/history methods cannot help.\n\n'
 model+='The largest eligible curve has592 independent training BO3,16/list; it does not establish performance at the original larger training sizes.\n\n'
 model+='The32/64/128 curves are unavailable because the user chose not to replace interrupted histories. Every reported family/seed uses the same original nested subset and fixed validation population.\n\n'
 model+='## Costs and reproducibility\n\nHistorical audit/conversion, new collection, feature extraction, fit process startup/CPU, validation inference, analysis, memory and storage are tracked separately. Complete recurring inference is timed separately on 16 fixed validation histories spanning all eight archetypes and both chooser assignments. It processes every legal callback and every genuine decision readout, including GRU updates and A/event features. Sampled validation-point inference cost is labelled separately and is not presented as full online cost. Complete fit/evaluation costs and model parameter counts are in per-fit and validation-result records. Reconciliation consists only of legal support masking/normalization and is included in inference timing. Offline label scoring/export time is not misrepresented as deployed inference.\n\n'
 evaluations=[read(p) for p in sorted((OUT/'validation-results').glob('*.json'))]
 if evaluations:
  charges={x['key']:x['CPU_seconds'] for x in rows(OUT/'fit-cost-ledger.jsonl')};model+='| Frozen model | Fit CPU min | Full online CPU s/BO3 | Incremental model CPU s/BO3 | Validation/scoring/export CPU min | Peak process MiB |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
  for e in evaluations:
   online=e.get('full_online_timing',{});model+=f'| {e["key"]} | {charges.get(e["key"],0)/60:.2f} | {fmt(online.get("complete_recurring_CPU_seconds_per_BO3"),3)} | {fmt(online.get("incremental_model_CPU_seconds_per_BO3"),3)} | {e["CPU_seconds"]/60:.2f} | {e["peak_RSS_kib"]/1024:.1f} |\n'
  model+='\nFull online timing is an actual streaming pass on all 16 fixed histories; per-callback recurrent-update and per-readout p50/p95 CPU latency are retained for every model. Peak memory is per process, not a fabricated aggregate simultaneous peak.\n\n'
 model+='Configuration and evidence: '+', '.join(link(n) for n in ('model-config.json','fit-schedule.json','schema.json','training-subsets.json','probe.json','feasibility-forecast.json','analysis.json','completion.json'))+'. The raw split, model source, SDK/policy/deck hashes and fitted-artifact checksums are retained. Test remains sealed.\n'
 MODEL_REPORT.write_text(model)
 status=R/'docs/STATUS.md';old=status.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');start='<!-- BELIEF-DATASET-V1 -->';end='<!-- BELIEF-DATASET-V1-END -->'
 if start in old:i=old.index(start);j=old.index(end,i)+len(end);old=old[:i]+old[j:].lstrip('\n')
 status.write_text(f'{start}\n## Reusable belief dataset and supervised learning curves\n\n{iso()}: **{state}**. {reason} Dataset committed {len(index)}/5920; eligible supervised fits {sum(x["state"]=="COMPLETE" for x in fits)}/14; original32/64/128 unavailable without replacements; locked-test scores0. [Dataset](../reports/astra-unown-belief-dataset-v1.md); [learning curves](../reports/astra-unown-belief-classifier-learning-curves.md).\n{end}\n\n'+old)
 mirror=Path('C:/path/to/ptcg-agent') if os.name=='nt' else Path('/path/to/ptcg-agent')
 paths=[DATA_REPORT,MODEL_REPORT,status]+[p for p in OUT.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ('.json','.jsonl','.md','.png')]
 for source in paths:
  target=mirror/source.relative_to(R);target.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);shutil.copy2(source,target)
